{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7F62F973967E3D294C41E0195794FEAC/jobs/483294": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty/Business Administration",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty/Business Administration You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty/Business Administration Nichols College - Dudley, MA 01571 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,550.00 - $4,250.00 Commission Apply Description Adjunct Faculty - Business Administration SCHOOL: School of Business POSITION TYPE: Adjunct / Part-Time Faculty JOB SUMMARY & REQUIREMENTS Nichols College is seeking qualified professionals and educators to join the adjunct faculty team in its AACSB-accredited School of Business. We welcome applications from individuals interested in teaching undergraduate and, where appropriate, graduate courses in Accounting, Business Analytics, Economics, Entrepreneurship, Finance, and Management. Course assignments vary by semester based on enrollment and program needs and may include introductory through advanced-level courses. As an adjunct faculty member, you will provide practical, engaging instruction that connects academic concepts with real-world business applications. Nichols College emphasizes experiential learning, professional preparation, and innovative teaching practices, and adjunct faculty are encouraged to draw upon their professional expertise in the classroom. Adjunct faculty positions are appointed on a course-by-course basis. Successful adjunct instructors may be considered for additional teaching opportunities in future semesters. RESPONSIBILITIES Prepare and deliver high-quality instruction aligned with established course learning objectives. Create an engaging and inclusive learning environment. Incorporate practical applications, examples, cases, projects, technology, and other experiential approaches where appropriate. Provide timely feedback and evaluation of student work. Maintain regular communication with students and appropriate College personnel. Submit grades and other required course information according to College deadlines. Participate in assessment or other academic activities related to assigned courses when appropriate. QUALIFICATIONS Required qualifications: Master's degree or higher in the discipline being taught or a closely related field. Demonstrated academic or professional expertise relevant to the teaching area. Ability to communicate effectively and engage students from a variety of academic and professional backgrounds. Preferred qualifications: Previous college-level teaching experience. Significant professional experience in the discipline. Experience incorporating technology, applied projects, case studies, simulations, or other experiential learning approaches into instruction. Terminal degree or relevant professional certification where appropriate to the discipline. Nichols College particularly values adjunct faculty who can bring current industry practices and professional experiences into the classroom. AREAS OF INTEREST Applicants should identify in their letter of interest the discipline(s) and types of courses they are qualified and interested in teaching. Accounting Financial accounting, managerial accounting, auditing, taxation, accounting information systems, and related areas. Business Analytics Data analytics, data visualization, business intelligence, statistics, database and data management, predictive analytics, and related areas. Economics Microeconomics, macroeconomics, managerial economics, international economics, and related areas. Entrepreneurship Entrepreneurship, new venture creation, innovation, small business management, family business, and related areas. Finance Corporate finance, investments, financial markets, financial planning, risk management, and related areas. Management Principles of management, organizational behavior, leadership, strategic management, operations, project management, and related areas. COLLEGE PROFILE Nichols College is a business-oriented institution with a strong emphasis on leadership, professional development, experiential learning, and career preparation. Located in Dudley, Massachusetts, Nichols provides students with a close-knit learning environment where faculty bring academic expertise and professional experience directly into the classroom. The Nichols College School of Business is accredited by AACSB International, reflecting a commitment to high standards of academic quality and continuous improvement in business education. Nichols College is institutionally accredited by the New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE). The College offers undergraduate and graduate programs designed to prepare students for professional success and continued growth throughout their careers. Nichols College is an Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. APPLICATION INFORMATION Please apply online and include the following materials: A letter of interest identifying the discipline(s) and types of courses you are interested in teaching. A current resume or curriculum vitae. The names and contact information of three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis as teaching needs arise. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7F62F973967E3D294C41E0195794FEAC/jobs/461376": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of English/Communications",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor of English/Communications You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Professor of English/Communications Nichols College - Dudley, MA 01571 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,550.00 - $3,550.00 Commission Apply Description Adjunct Professor of English/Communications DEPARTMENT:  English/Communications TERM: 2026 Fall Semester JOB SUMMARY & REQUIREMENTS: Nichols College, a business-oriented, four-year College, is seeking a strong teacher to join our adjunct/part time faculty team, to begin Fall 2026. Openings include in-person sections of our first-year course College Writing and first-year course Effective Speaking, with other sections potentially available based on enrollment. As an adjunct faculty member, you'll provide practical hands-on instruction in an engaging learning environment, incorporating innovative teaching methodologies. Adjunct faculty positions are appointed on a course-by-course basis. A successful adjunct may be appointed for future semesters. The successful candidate is expected to have: Master’s degree (or higher) in English, Communications, or a related discipline. Previous teaching experience, college level preferred College Profile: Nichols College is a college of choice for business and leadership education with a distinctive focus on professional development and the pursuit of passion.  The picturesque 200-acre campus is located in the town of Dudley, a rural New England Community one hour from Boston, Harford and Providence.  The College has 1200 undergraduates and 200 graduate students, and a diverse faculty. Founded in 1815, Nichols is a private, primarily 4-year undergraduate business school offering a Bachelor of Science in Business Administration with 20 concentrations. The College also offers 7 Bachelor of Arts degrees, as well as 4 graduate degrees: MBA, MSA, Master of Science in Organizational Leadership and Master of Science in Counterterrorism. Nichols is NECHE and IACBE accredited; additionally, the Sport Management program is COSMA accredited. Nichols College is an Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer and encourages women and BIPOC to apply.  Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. APPLICATION INFORMATION: Please apply online and include a letter of interest, resume, and the names of three professional references. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7F62F973967E3D294C41E0195794FEAC/jobs/460418": {
      "title": "Creative Design Specialist",
      "description": "Creative Design Specialist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Creative Design Specialist Nichols College - Dudley, MA 01571 Apply Overview Salary Range $60,000.00 - $60,000.00 Salary Apply Description Job Title                 Creative Design Specialist Department          Marketing and Communications Supervisor             Vice President for Marketing and Communications Job Purpose          The Creative Design Specialist contributes to the college’s financial success through the creation and delivery of compelling print and digital design materials and other outputs. As the college’s primary designer, the Specialist works closely with enrollment (admissions) and other key campus partners to communicate the value of a Nichols College education and contribute to strategic growth priorities. The Specialist helps meet tactical objectives in alignment with the institution’s marketing and communications goals, and produces tangible assets and collateral while adhering to brand standards. Job Duties : Design multipage publications, brochures, newsletters, fact (one) sheets, multi-media displays, billboards, digital and print advertisements, and other long-form publications Develop original print and web graphics, illustrations, charts, graphs, webpages and artwork for use in digital and print marketing and communications, including nichols.edu Capture, edit and optimize photography; photograph key institutional events such as Commencement, Convocation, new student orientation, etc.; manage college’s digital asset management (DAM) resource Identify and advise print vendors; ensure product quality and timeliness of printed communication materials and publications; determine standards and most efficient methods of production to consider timeframes and/or cost; evaluate finished product and analyze success of products Follow established graphic and branding standards to elevate the Nichols College brand and ensure all materials are visually consistent, professional, and aligned with brand guidelines. Ensure accurate use of logos, colors, typography, and layouts across all deliverables and campus-wide departments Possess strong working knowledge of graphic design and productivity software, including Adobe Creative Cloud, WordPress, Figma, Canva, Microsoft Office, including PowerPoint, etc. Research and manage stock photography and video; manage creative and digital graphics subscriptions; work with outside photographers, including Nichols College student staff; manage work study students as necessary Maintain an archive of finished creative design projects, timelines and calendars, and other project management tools and resources Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferably in graphic design, digital communications, or a related field; or technical certification and relevant professional experience in creative and graphic design High proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud Pro and Microsoft Office; working knowledge of WordPress, Figma, Canva Knowledge of best-practice design techniques, tools and principles Strong portfolio of published work, including graphic design, digital marketing, multimedia and photography Demonstrated creativity and originality Effective time management skills and ability to juggle multiple projects concurrently Adaptability and flexibility, including evening/weekend availability Additional duties as assigned Physical Job Components: Light to moderate lifting of equipment, supplies and other materials Able to use office and telecommunications equipment Walking is required, traveling may be expected at times Ability to communicate in writing and orally Application Information: Please send resume, cover letter and salary requirements to: Department of Human Resources Nichols College 121 Center Road Dudley, MA 01571 humanresources@nichols.edu Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7F62F973967E3D294C41E0195794FEAC/jobs/419487": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for Men's Volleyball",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant for Men's Volleyball You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Graduate Assistant for Men's Volleyball Nichols College - Dudley, MA 01571 Apply Overview Salary Range $10,000.00 - $10,000.00 Commission Apply Description JOB DESCRIPTION: Graduate Assistant Coach for Men’s Volleyball DATE: April 7, 2026 DEPARTMENT: Division of Athletics REPORTS TO: Head Coach JOB SUMMARY : Nichols College, a member of the NCAA Division III, located in Dudley, MA (Central MA) invites applications for a Graduate Assistant position with the men’s volleyball program. The position begins August 2026. A bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university is required. Candidates will need to apply to the Nichols College Graduate Studies Program. This position also includes a stipend - $10,000. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Assist in meeting recruitment goals established by the Division of Athletics and Head Coach. Assist the Head Coach in planning and executing practices. Assist in game and practice day set-up. Attend all practices and games. Support current student-athlete academic success. Manage social media platforms. Serve as the travel coordinator (meals and travel operations). Assist with all areas of video operations. Engage with Athletic Communications staff for events, game days, etc. Help with equipment/uniform inventory, distribution, and collection. Assist with fundraising and alumni outreach. Supervise team managers. Attain driving certification with the College. Be an active member of the Division of Athletics (attend meetings, scheduled campus events, etc.). Assist with game management duties out of season. Work the fitness room desk while in and out of season, 1-2 days a week. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND EDUCATION REQUIRED: Bachelor’s degree preferred with experience in collegiate athletics. Genuine understanding and commitment to NCAA Division III intercollegiate athletics philosophy. Solid knowledge and technical skills for the sport of volleyball. Must have strong leadership and people skills, plus an ability to work with all constituencies of the campus. Able to identify and attract outstanding student athletes to Nichols College. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to handle a multi-task work environment. Computer proficiency. Valid driver’s license and good driving record. Light lifting. Ability to work extended hours, including evenings and weekends. BENEFITS: Stipend$10,000 Graduate tuition remission On-campus housing with application Use of fitness center PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: CPR/AED and First Aid certification Coaching experience Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7F62F973967E3D294C41E0195794FEAC/jobs/324799": {
      "title": "Part Time Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Part Time Public Safety Officer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Part Time Public Safety Officer Nichols College - Dudley, MA 01571 Apply Overview Salary Range $18.00 - $18.25 Hourly Apply Description Preferred evening and overnight coverage Will hire as needed Summary of Position: Under the direction of the Director of Public Safety or their designee, the Public Safety Officer performs duties to ensure the safety and security on the campus for students, staff, faculty and visitors. Applies crime risk and safety hazard prevention techniques, methods, practices, and enforces College policies and procedures. Public Safety Officers monitor the security of the buildings and surrounding areas of the campus. They may also serve as liaison between external law enforcement agencies and the campus community. Essential Job Functions: Patrols and secures campus grounds and facilities by vehicle and foot. Assists in the protection of life and property on campus. Examines doors, windows, gates, roadways, and lighting to ensure security. Investigates and submits reports concerning criminal offenses committed on the campus. Prepares written reports as required. Completes and maintains records of daily activities including a Communication Log sheet with calls for service and building checks. Monitors and reports on a continual basis all conditions which may create security or safety hazards on the College property. Monitors the camera system to ensure there is no criminal activity at other parts of the campus. Contacts law enforcement, fire, or other public agencies as required. Assists public service representatives including fire, medical, and police with directions to emergency investigations. Enforces College and local laws, rules, ordinances, and regulations according to established procedures. Answers incoming calls to Public Safety and dispatches information by radio to officers. Provides information and directions to campus facilities, events, or other locations. Monitors campus traffic and parking; issue citations for violations. Provides crowd and traffic control for special events on and off campus. Responds to complaints from the campus community and assists parties to resolve issues as appropriate. Respond and perform access control duties including securing and/or unlocking academic buildings for faculty, staff and students Respond to fire, smoke detector, and security alarms Provide safety escorts Fill front desk assignments Answer calls for service Receive and fill out property receipts for lost and found items May provide first responder support for fires and/or first aid needs. Other duties as assigned Work Environment & Physical Demands This position is an essential personnel position which requires working in a variety of situations including during holidays, weekends, day/evening/night shifts, forced overtime, and in a state of emergency Must be able to: sit or stand for long periods of time; walk, run, climb, bend, stoop and lift weights proportionate with need to perform medical assistance; wear a uniform and equipment, and operate a motor vehicle Lifting, pulling, or pushing heavy objects up to 30 lbs. Prolonged periods of sitting, standing, walking Bending at the waist, kneeling or crouching Must be able to traverse all types of terrain including up and down hills, and on off road uneven surfaces Environment: Indoor and outdoor environment. Seasonal heat and cold or adverse weather conditions May be exposed to uncomfortable work spaces such as darkness or poor lighting, dirt/dust, fumes/odors, isolation, mechanical or traffic hazards. May be exposed to unpleasant social situations or hostile community response Must remain calm and be able to deescalate volatile situations Driving a vehicle to conduct work Skills/Abilities: Read, write and speak English fluently Willing to work varying shifts and flexible hours, including weekends and holidays Solid communication and interpersonal skills Must be customer service oriented. Detect problems and report accurate information to appropriate staff React in an emergency and make sound, rational decisions. Work in high stress, confrontational or hostile environments Solid critical things and problem-solving skills Work in crews or independently Understand and follow directions and complete work assignments on schedule Understand and follow oral and written instructions Take appropriate steps to promote and sustain effective working relationships within a diverse multicultural environment Education and Training: High school diploma or GED At least 1 year of directly related experience which may include directly related certification or practicum training Must have a valid driver's license and safe driving record. Must have CPR and First Aid certification within 6 months of hire Will be required to pass a comprehensive background check and drug screening. This position description is not intended to contain a comprehensive list of activities, duties, or responsibilities. Additional duties may be assigned based on business operational needs. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
